{
 "page": {
  "title": "How a trierarch works",
  "heading": "How a trierarch keeps your ships crewed",
  "kicker": "Explainer · 2 min · voice and music",
  "aria": "Animated explainer of the Aeolus trierarch. By hand, the operator crews three ships with four steps each (pick a computer, make a worktree, start the session, paste the crew line with its secret), and restarts a session that ended at night: thirteen steps. With a trierarch: the trierarch plugin beside the fleet picks a computer for each crew request, and a trierarch on each computer, a plain process, makes the worktree, registers so the session never sees the secret, starts the session, wakes it when a message arrives, restarts it when it ends, tells the owner after five restarts in an hour, and releases the ship when its request is removed. Use it when ships must stay crewed with no one watching, when sessions spread over several computers, and to have worktrees and secrets handled; skip it for a ship or two you crew yourself, in a chat client, or on Windows."
 },
